data.content:
Your code **doesn't use `Thread.Abort`**, so it won't throw `PlatformNotSupportedException` on .NET 8. However, it does use raw `Thread` which is generally replaced with modern patterns in .NET 8.

## Migration Guidance

**`Thread.Abort` in .NET 8:** It throws `PlatformNotSupportedException`. The replacement is cooperative cancellation via `CancellationToken`.

**Recommended rewrite using `Task` + cancellation:**

```csharp
public class SimpleWorker
{
    public async Task RunBatchAsync(List<WorkItem> items, CancellationToken ct = default)
    {
        var tasks = items.Select(item => Task.Run(() => Process(item, ct), ct));
        await Task.WhenAll(tasks);
    }

    private void Process(WorkItem item, CancellationToken ct)
    {
        ct.ThrowIfCancellationRequested();
        Thread.Sleep(100); // replace with: await Task.Delay(100, ct) if async
        item.Result = ComputeResult(item.Input);
    }
}
```

**Key migration rules:**

| .NET Framework | .NET 8 Replacement |
|---|---|
| `Thread.Abort()` | `CancellationTokenSource.Cancel()` |
| `ThreadAbortException` catch | `OperationCanceledException` catch |
| `Thread.ResetAbort()` | Remove (not needed) |
| `Thread.Sleep` | `await Task.Delay(ms, ct)` |
| Raw `Thread` + `Join` | `Task.Run` + `Task.WhenAll` |

Your code is safe to migrate as-is, but switching to `Task.Run` gives you structured cancellation support if you need to abort work later.
